{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 468716, "name": "Bryan Moore", "username": "bryanmoore", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bryanmoore/{size}/1993_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T17:58:38.753Z", "cooked": "<p>The title kind of says it all… I’m looking for if there is a method by which I can automatically identify unnecessary, unneeded, and unused packages; e.g., I noticed during a recent update that <code>libva-intel-media-driver</code> was being updated, but my system has no need for anything Intel related because I am pure AMD.</p>\n<p>Thanks for all the help!</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T19:06:08.166Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1070, "reads": 47, "readers_count": 46, "score": 5339.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Bryan Moore", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1978, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468727, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T19:25:05.937Z", "cooked": "<p>Not an automatic way but some things to check.</p>\n<p>To see what autoremove would get rid of<br>\n<code>dnf list --autoremove</code></p>\n<p>User installed packages sorted by date<br>\n<code>dnf repoquery --userinstalled --qf=\"%{installtime} %{full_nevra}\\n\" | awk '{print strftime(\" %F-%H:%M:%S \", $1)\"\\t\" $2}' | sort -r -h</code></p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T19:25:49.399Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 16, "reads": 44, "readers_count": 43, "score": 88.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468731, "name": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "username": "glb", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/glb/{size}/570_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T19:36:15.937Z", "cooked": "<p>Also not automatic, but <code>rpmreaper</code> will help to identify “leaf” packages that no other package depends on and which can (probably) be removed without much consequence. It also has a quick way of getting summaries of what various packages are as you navigate through them (press the <kbd>i</kbd> key).</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T19:36:15.937Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 44, "readers_count": 43, "score": 28.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 586, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "user_status": {"description": "chill'n", "emoji": "coffee", "ends_at": null, "message_bus_last_id": 1}, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "eureka", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468735, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T19:48:14.583Z", "cooked": "<p>This is a cool tool Thanks!!!</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T19:48:14.583Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 7, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 43.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 586, "username": "glb", "name": "Gregory Lee Bartholomew", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/glb/{size}/570_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468745, "name": "Bryan Moore", "username": "bryanmoore", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bryanmoore/{size}/1993_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T20:50:34.527Z", "cooked": "<p>I “autoremove” pretty regularly and think that’s a great suggestion; I also think <code>rpmreaper</code> is a cool tool and need to learn more about it.</p>\n<p>I’m not sure either of those suggestions actually addresses what I’m getting at, so I don’t think I was clear…</p>\n<p>In my mind, I’m imagining (read: hoping) there is a tool that will use my current system configuration and identify those packages that are installed that aren’t necessarily “compatible.” For example, the tool will identify that I don’t have any Intel parts and recommend all the Intel packages that were installed at any point for removal.</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T20:50:34.527Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5, "reads": 38, "readers_count": 37, "score": 37.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Bryan Moore", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1978, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468753, "name": "Barry A Scott", "username": "barryascott", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/db3279/{size}.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T22:22:00.706Z", "cooked": "<p>Hardware firmware is installed by defaiult. In that way it makes it possible to ungrade your hardware and keep working. It also makes it possible to move the disk to a new system.</p>\n<p>As the packages take up little space on my disks I’ve not been interested in remove these types of packages.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T22:22:00.706Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 11, "reads": 32, "readers_count": 31, "score": 61.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Barry A Scott", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Building the Outer Ring (Copr Build VI)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4115, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468771, "name": "Espionage724", "username": "Espionage724", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/espionage724/{size}/6543_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T23:12:47.877Z", "cooked": "<p>I’m pretty sure unnecessary firmware was being put into <code>initramfs</code> (longer generation, slower boot); I think omitting through <code>dracut.conf</code> would work vs removing packages, but I did this on an all-Intel laptop:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf remove 'amd-gpu-firmware' 'nvidia-gpu-firmware' 'atheros-firmware' 'mt7xxx-firmware'\n</code></pre>\n<p>I was surprised to see Anaconda installer stuff present post-install, and don’t do anything with virtualization (iirc there’s a lot of unnecessary dependencies):</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">sudo dnf remove libvirt-client anaconda-*\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T23:12:47.877Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 26.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Espionage724", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 3487, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/8", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468777, "name": "Joe Walker", "username": "grumpey", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/grumpey/{size}/54040_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-28T23:51:43.759Z", "cooked": "<p>what if you did it with an excludes drop in file …</p>\n<p><code>/etc/dnf/libdnf5.conf.d/90-unwantedpkgs.conf </code></p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">[main]\nexcludepkgs=\"akmod-nvidia, akmod-nvidia-390xx, akmod-nvidia-470xx\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>and then just used something like ..</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">#!/usr/bin/env bash\nUNWANTEDPKGS=\"$(sed -e '1d' -e 's/\"//g' -e 's/,//g' -e's/excludepkgs=//' /etc/dnf/libdnf5.conf.d/90-unwantedpkgs.conf)\"\nfor pkg in ${UNWANTEDPKGS}\ndo\n  echo \"${pkg}\"\n  dnf --exclude=\"\" list --installed \"${pkg}\"\ndone \n</code></pre>", "post_number": 9, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-28T23:52:13.249Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 21.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Joe Walker", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Curious Penguin (Ask Fedora IV)", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 1978, "username": "bryanmoore", "name": "Bryan Moore", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bryanmoore/{size}/1993_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 638, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/9", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 468849, "name": "Bryan Moore", "username": "bryanmoore", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/bryanmoore/{size}/1993_2.png", "created_at": "2025-12-29T13:50:45.445Z", "cooked": "<p>Both of those ideas sound interesting… Since it looks like I’d be setting up my own scripts and/or altering the way dnf behaves, it sounds like there is <em>not</em> an already existing tool like that which I described.</p>", "post_number": 10, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2025-12-29T13:50:45.445Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 8, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 43.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 178621, "topic_slug": "method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages", "display_username": "Bryan Moore", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1978, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/method-to-automatically-remove-unneeded-packages/178621/10", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [468716, 468727, 468731, 468735, 468745, 468753, 468771, 468777, 468849]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 311], [4, 310]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags":